    "speaker": "host2",
    "text": "The Kuleshov effect is this fascinating psychological phenomenon in film where viewers derive more meaning from the interaction of two sequential shots than from either shot alone. It’s named after Soviet filmmaker Lev Kuleshov, who, back in the 1910s and 20s, conducted an experiment that basically showed how editing shapes emotion.",
    "type": "listener_request"
  },
