    "speaker": "host2",
    "text": "It really is fascinating. So, the Kuleshov Effect is named after Soviet filmmaker Lev Kuleshov back in the early 1920s. He conducted this famous experiment where he edited shots of actor Ivan Mozhukhin's neutral face next to different objects: a bowl of soup, a dead woman, and a playful child.",
    "type": "deep_dive"
  },
